WEBVTT

00:07:57.739 --> 00:08:00.393
PA: Our work is in a long line
of cultural organizers

00:08:00.417 --> 00:08:04.511
that understood to use art
to animate a radical future.

00:08:04.535 --> 00:08:06.325
Artists like June Jordan,

00:08:06.349 --> 00:08:07.993
Emory Douglas

00:08:08.017 --> 00:08:09.292
and Nina Simone.

00:08:09.316 --> 00:08:12.553
They understood what many of us
are just now realizing --

00:08:12.577 --> 00:08:14.393
that to get people to build the ship,

00:08:14.417 --> 00:08:16.459
you've got to get
them to long for the sea;

00:08:16.483 --> 00:08:20.721
that data rarely moves people,
but great art always does.

00:08:20.745 --> 00:08:21.965
This understanding --

00:08:21.989 --> 00:08:24.445
(Applause)

00:08:24.469 --> 00:08:26.386
This understanding informed the thinking

00:08:26.410 --> 00:08:28.576
behind the Dream Defenders'
"Freedom Papers,"

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.789
a radical political vision
for the future of Florida